1
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,260
I'm so glad you found it for me.

2
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:08,860
I did find the seal,

3
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:11,970
but I didn't know where the key was.

4
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,070
But... why...

5
00:00:15,870 --> 00:00:18,210
are you... here?

6
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:21,570
You seem surprised.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,220
You see, this seal is what we were after,

8
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:30,540
so my being here is really 
a matter of course.

9
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:05,180
Why... are you... here?

10
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:08,390
Oh, I'm sorry.

11
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:13,900
I suppose it is Bishop Romanée-Conti and 
your mother that you wanted to know about.

12
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,460
You need not worry.

13
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:22,530
The two you are so worried about, 
Bishop Romanée-Conti and your mother, are safe.

14
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:23,910
R-Really?

15
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:25,980
Yes, really.

16
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:30,540
Neither the worshipers nor 
I wish to cause harm to anyone.

17
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,000
What we seek is this seal.

18
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:39,010
So when you're done with the seal,
 will you leave the forest?

19
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:42,550
You'll go without doing anything 
mean to the people here?

20
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,400
Yes, of course.

21
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:48,560
We do not wish to make any 
unnecessary sacrifices.

22
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,810
So, please give me the key now.

23
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:54,020
The... key?

24
00:02:54,290 --> 00:02:56,360
Yes, the key.

25
00:02:56,820 --> 00:03:00,390
Given that this seal is shaped like a door,

26
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:02,110
it will not open without the key.

27
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:06,380
And I believe the key is in your possession.

28
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:08,330
I don't know anything about that!

29
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,510
Hiding it would not be very wise.

30
00:03:11,510 --> 00:03:15,470
I-I'm not! I really, really don't know!

31
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:16,880
I don't have any key!

32
00:03:17,210 --> 00:03:18,750
Nobody gave me one!

33
00:03:19,790 --> 00:03:21,220
I see.

34
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:26,640
Then I will have to turn this entire 
forest over until I find it.

35
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:30,560
I-I'll open it! I'll open the seal!

36
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:34,300
Oh, you will? That's wonderful.

37
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:38,080
So you really do have the key, then.

38
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,030
After all, it is obvious...

39
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:44,700
that you are the witch's daughter.

40
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,930
Witch?

41
00:03:46,930 --> 00:03:49,580
Now, the seal, please.

42
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:54,490
As soon as the door is open, we will leave.

43
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:13,060
Consider yourself to be the key.

44
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:20,620
I'm... the key.

45
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:33,560
Can you see it now?

46
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:35,990
You can't see it?

47
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:38,890
No, I cannot.

48
00:04:39,450 --> 00:04:43,740
That key is only given to the 
one qualified to possess it.

49
00:04:45,570 --> 00:04:47,340
Go on, open it.

50
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,560
Then your wish will be granted.

51
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,150
<i>Promise me, Emilia...</i>

52
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:01,070
I... I can't open it.

53
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:01,820
Why?

54
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:05,710
I made... I made a promise.

55
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:09,710
I see. Well, promises are very important.

56
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:13,060
A promise with your mother, I'm sure.

57
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:17,630
But there are times when 
a decision must be made,

58
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:20,530
even if it means breaking a promise.

59
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:24,150
Which hope do you seek?

60
00:05:24,690 --> 00:05:26,840
Which... hope?

61
00:05:27,090 --> 00:05:29,590
One is the hope that you 
will keep your promise,

62
00:05:29,590 --> 00:05:33,600
get us to leave, and overcome this hardship.

63
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:38,850
The other is the hope that you will 
resolve all this harmoniously

64
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:42,320
by breaking your promise 
and opening the seal.

65
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:45,580
Which fate will you choose?

66
00:05:46,150 --> 00:05:48,530
I will entrust fate to you.

67
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:57,210
I promised Mother.

68
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,720
I'm going to keep my promise.

69
00:06:01,590 --> 00:06:03,950
I will. So...

70
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,100
Mother...

71
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:12,210
You trust your mother, 
your guiding light, to the very end.

72
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:17,620
That answer is the decision 
your soul has led you to.

73
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:19,780
I shall respect that.

74
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:27,690
So you must also respect my 
decision to open this seal

75
00:06:28,330 --> 00:06:30,260
by any means necessary.

76
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,990
Pandora!

77
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:36,250
It's dangerous to attack without 
observing your surround—

78
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:37,750
Take this!

79
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,590
Emilia?!

80
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:47,180
But why? You should be out of the forest!

81
00:06:48,130 --> 00:06:52,020
Do you not find it cruel to ask her why?

82
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:57,580
She came here out of concern for you, 
because she wished to help you.

83
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,630
When you both wear the same expression,

84
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:03,870
the resemblance between you is even clearer.

85
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:05,940
Truly mother and daughter.

86
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,570
I'm not Emilia's mother!

87
00:07:08,570 --> 00:07:11,030
She gets her cute face 
from my sister-in-law!

88
00:07:11,030 --> 00:07:15,200
Ah, her? Please forgive me, then.

89
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:20,370
Her real parents must be so pleased.

90
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:26,110
Don't you dare speak of my 
brother or sister-in-law!

91
00:07:26,770 --> 00:07:31,430
Simply rampaging and refusing 
to talk will only tire you out.

92
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:33,590
You should calm down...

93
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:37,810
so that we have a chance to discuss—

94
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:38,400
I'm telling you to give it a rest!

95
00:07:39,610 --> 00:07:42,770
Emilia! Wait, no! I didn't mean to—

96
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:48,670
Can you not direct even a tiny bit of 
that emotion to the one you despise?

97
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:56,370
I will not tell you to love all 
people as you love your daughter.

98
00:07:56,850 --> 00:08:00,240
But there are things that can change 
with just a bit of sympathy.

99
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,330
Don't be ridiculous!

100
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:04,560
Who would... Who would listen to you?!

101
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,690
Then why not try this?

102
00:08:06,690 --> 00:08:10,720
Convince your daughter with your own words.

103
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:14,610
I have verified that she possesses the key,

104
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:18,310
but she shows no desire to 
open the door for me...

105
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:22,050
Because she wishes to 
keep her promise to you.

106
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:27,180
I promise you that if the seal is opened,

107
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:31,860
we will leave this forest 
and do nothing further.

108
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:37,020
"Promise" is such a nice word, isn't it?

109
00:08:40,430 --> 00:08:45,040
I'm sorry you had to go 
through this, Emilia.

110
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:47,740
Are you the only one here?

111
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:49,500
Where's Archi?

112
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:54,260
Archi told me to run toward 
the white flowers...

113
00:08:56,350 --> 00:08:58,990
So I just ran.

114
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:06,690
Emilia...

115
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:09,110
Emilia...

116
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:12,530
Thank you for keeping your promise.

117
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,330
What a good girl.

118
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,090
What a good girl.

119
00:09:16,610 --> 00:09:17,550
Mother...

120
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,570
Mother...

121
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:23,310
I... I...

122
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:24,700
Emilia...

123
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,080
I'm so proud of you.

124
00:09:28,730 --> 00:09:30,350
You are my treasure.

125
00:09:32,470 --> 00:09:35,970
What beautiful motherly love.
I'm deeply moved.

126
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:40,910
Truly, how wonderful it is to see such love.

127
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:45,630
I won't open the seal, 
and I won't let you have her.

128
00:09:46,050 --> 00:09:46,890
And you...

129
00:09:47,770 --> 00:09:50,150
will turn into an ice statue and die!

130
00:09:53,250 --> 00:09:55,440
I finally caught up to you!

131
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:56,740
Geuse!

132
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:57,570
Fortuna-sama!

133
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,200
Al Huma!

134
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:04,080
Unseen Hand!

135
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:14,880
Mother?

136
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,660
And now, it is... over!

137
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:45,980
That should be more than enough this time!

138
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:49,250
Fortuna-sama, be careful! 
Keep your guard up!

139
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:51,200
I will make sure that...

140
00:10:54,890 --> 00:10:56,050
Geuse?

141
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,510
Emilia-sama?

142
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:03,420
No... It can't be!

143
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:11,560
It was not your fault. 
You mistook what you saw.

144
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:13,560
That is all.

145
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:24,250
This can't be!

146
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:28,410
This can't be! This can't be! 
This can't be! This can't be!

147
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:33,200
What... What am I... What am I doing?!

148
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,530
What have I...

149
00:11:34,530 --> 00:11:38,130
Why?! Why?! Why?! Why?! 
Why?! Why?! Why?! Why?!

150
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:41,090
Why did I do this?!

151
00:11:41,650 --> 00:11:44,050
It was all for love.

152
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:50,190
You offered up your very soul 
to save the one you love.

153
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:53,870
All that you have done was out of love.

154
00:11:53,870 --> 00:11:56,770
A beautiful, wonderful symbol of love...

155
00:11:56,770 --> 00:12:01,790
Love... Love... Love... Love... Love...

156
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:04,360
Yes, there is nothing to fear,
 nothing to regret.

157
00:12:01,790 --> 00:12:04,360
Love... Love...

158
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:09,950
This is the inevitability that the 
path you have walked was leading to.

159
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:13,280
Your love is not wrong.

160
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:16,750
For... love...

161
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:23,090
Emilia...

162
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:24,800
Mother?

163
00:12:25,310 --> 00:12:26,470
Brother...

164
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:28,980
I'm sorry...

165
00:12:29,590 --> 00:12:30,560
Mother...

166
00:12:30,940 --> 00:12:36,630
I couldn't do... any of the 
things... you told me to do.

167
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,180
Your wife...

168
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:41,080
will be so angry.

169
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:45,040
She'll never... forgive me.

170
00:12:59,110 --> 00:13:02,240
I'll forgive you, Mother.

171
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:06,560
You are my mother.

172
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:09,220
You've always taken care of me.

173
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:16,480
You loved me just as much 
as my mom and dad did.

174
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:21,940
So there's nothing you need 
to apologize for. Nothing.

175
00:13:22,710 --> 00:13:30,390
Emilia will always... always love you,
 Mother Fortuna.

176
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:32,940
I love you...

177
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:35,310
I love you... I love you.

178
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,160
I love you!

179
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:43,710
Lia...

180
00:13:45,670 --> 00:13:46,700
Mother?

181
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:54,810
My little crybaby...

182
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,990
I love you... so, so much.

183
00:14:09,570 --> 00:14:14,450
Now, are you ready to choose the 
hope that you will break the seal?

184
00:14:15,150 --> 00:14:17,290
Open... the seal?

185
00:14:17,670 --> 00:14:22,610
The mother you made your promise to,
 sadly, has passed away.

186
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:27,760
You are no longer shackled by any promises.

187
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,590
What do you say?

188
00:14:50,290 --> 00:14:51,320
Die.

189
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:58,120
What a dangerous thing 
to do. What brought—

190
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,120
Die.

191
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,000
Please calm down.

192
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:04,350
We can talk it over until you under—

193
00:15:04,350 --> 00:15:05,130
Die.

194
00:15:06,350 --> 00:15:08,880
You are a kind-hearted child.

195
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:10,800
Your mother would be sad if you—

196
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,390
Die.

197
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:15,250
What a problem. It seems to be 
having the opposite effect.

198
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:20,810
Die! Die! Die! Die!

199
00:15:21,270 --> 00:15:25,790
Die! Die! Die! Die!

200
00:15:25,790 --> 00:15:28,460
It is a shame when my long-desired 
wish is so close,

201
00:15:25,790 --> 00:15:28,460
Die! Die! Die! Die!

202
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:30,690
but it's time to end this for today.

203
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:34,870
Die! Die! Die! Die! Die! Die!

204
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:34,870
To continue further might force 
you into the impossible.

205
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:36,660
Die! Die!

206
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:44,450
Die! Die! Die! Die!

207
00:15:44,450 --> 00:15:49,590
At the rate you're going, you will 
likely fall into a deep sleep soon.

208
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:49,590
Die! Die! Die! Die!

209
00:15:49,590 --> 00:15:51,300
Die! Die! Die!

210
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:55,680
Your power will envelop this forest 
with frozen soil that will never thaw.

211
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:53,050
Die! Die...

212
00:15:53,050 --> 00:15:54,010
Die...

213
00:15:54,010 --> 00:15:54,970
Die...

214
00:15:56,510 --> 00:15:59,060
Either your mana will eventually run dry...

215
00:16:00,210 --> 00:16:06,330
Or it will be offset by someone 
with power comparable to yours.

216
00:16:07,370 --> 00:16:08,480
Until then...

217
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:12,450
Die! Die! Die! Die!

218
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,450
Unfortunately for you, I will not die.

219
00:16:12,450 --> 00:16:20,410
Die! Die! Die! Die! Die! Die!

220
00:16:13,230 --> 00:16:18,100
As surely as the snow melts 
and the glacial period ends,

221
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:20,410
you and I will meet again.

222
00:16:20,410 --> 00:16:25,210
Die! Die! Die!

223
00:16:21,030 --> 00:16:25,210
But it would make me sad if 
you still hated me then.

224
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:29,210
Die! Die! Die!

225
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:34,540
So your memories thus far will end with today,
as you forget my existence.

226
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:33,720
Die! Die! Die...

227
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:38,530
Fill the emptiness however you please.

228
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:43,610
Yes, you did your very best 
to keep your promise.

229
00:16:44,010 --> 00:16:47,220
I would be most pleased if you would 
engrave that fact in your heart,

230
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:50,980
and forever stay as you are now.

231
00:16:57,670 --> 00:17:01,160
I look forward to the day we meet again.

232
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:36,790
Mother...

233
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:49,130
If you blame yourself for the 
falsification of your memories,

234
00:17:49,130 --> 00:17:51,380
you are barking up the wrong tree.

235
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,780
The one you saw then was 
the Witch of Vanity.

236
00:17:56,370 --> 00:18:00,510
There's no doubt that her Authority of 
Vanity padded out your distorted memories.

237
00:18:01,410 --> 00:18:04,340
If I ask you about Pandora, 
will you tell me?

238
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:08,870
I seek out conversations with others,

239
00:18:08,870 --> 00:18:11,740
but in your case, I have no 
interest in digressions.

240
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,480
I see. Thank you.

241
00:18:16,330 --> 00:18:18,700
I was the one who turned them all into ice,

242
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:23,410
and it was when they were 
trying to save me.

243
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:27,980
By recalling the past, 
you saw the end of your regret.

244
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:31,520
All that remains is to give your answer.

245
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:33,710
My answer to the trial?

246
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:39,580
The first trial is completed by 
parting with your greatest regret.

247
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:43,710
It comes when you either accept 
or reject your past self.

248
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:50,340
The fact remains that your own sin caused

249
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:55,070
your mother, your friends, and your 
family to turn into ice statues.

250
00:18:56,290 --> 00:19:00,780
Your determination to save them 
can't even be called idealistic.

251
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:02,820
It was no more than a dream.

252
00:19:06,150 --> 00:19:08,780
So what is left for you?

253
00:19:15,530 --> 00:19:18,630
I've already been told that.

254
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,970
Mother loved me.

255
00:19:24,730 --> 00:19:29,350
I wanted to save my mother...
 Mother Fortuna.

256
00:19:30,330 --> 00:19:33,980
I wanted to sleep in her arms again,
 together in the same bed.

257
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:38,360
I wanted to tell her over 
and over that I loved her.

258
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,670
Are you saying you regret that?

259
00:19:41,050 --> 00:19:42,910
No, I don't regret it.

260
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:49,100
I don't regret keeping my promise 
and refusing to yield back then.

261
00:19:49,810 --> 00:19:54,770
If I regret anything, 
it's that I wasn't strong enough,

262
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,280
that I wasn't smart enough to do better.

263
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:05,600
But I'll never regret not breaking my 
promise with Mother to do as Pandora said.

264
00:20:06,510 --> 00:20:07,140
Because...

265
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:11,110
Mother told me in the very end

266
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:15,040
that she was proud of me 
for keeping my promise.

267
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,400
That I was her treasure.

268
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:23,780
Since you can't save her, doesn't that 
mean you've lost your reason to fight?

269
00:20:24,270 --> 00:20:25,890
Not at all.

270
00:20:25,890 --> 00:20:27,120
I couldn't save Mother,

271
00:20:27,710 --> 00:20:30,490
but I can't say that for certain 
about everyone else yet.

272
00:20:31,050 --> 00:20:35,040
They're still sleeping within 
the ice, waiting for me.

273
00:20:35,650 --> 00:20:38,010
Only I can save them.

274
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:40,750
The forest has been contaminated 
by the Black Serpent.

275
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:45,890
What if their bodies are corroded by disease,
 even if the frozen soil thaws?

276
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:50,000
What if none of the land your people 
owned for generations remains?

277
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,720
That's just imagining the worst.

278
00:20:52,610 --> 00:20:54,480
They're all waiting to be saved.

279
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:57,870
I need to wake them up soon 
and let them yell at me.

280
00:20:57,870 --> 00:21:01,070
Then they'll smile and tell me 
they're glad I'm still alive.

281
00:21:01,370 --> 00:21:02,650
What a foolish delusion.

282
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,910
No, it's the prediction of a happy future!

283
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:10,240
Mother said that, one day,

284
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,160
we would all leave the forest 
and live normal lives.

285
00:21:12,620 --> 00:21:15,920
Just like how we were friends 
with Geuse and his people,

286
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:18,760
and just like how Subaru said he loved me,

287
00:21:19,530 --> 00:21:24,300
the world where Mother and Geuse should 
have walked side by side will come!

288
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:28,650
And the villagers who turned 
into ice statues are there?

289
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:31,310
The ones that <i>you</i> froze?

290
00:21:31,730 --> 00:21:33,210
I'll apologize like crazy.

291
00:21:33,610 --> 00:21:37,240
I'll apologize over and over 
until they forgive me.

292
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:42,430
Then, once they forgive me, 
I'll show them the world.

293
00:21:42,430 --> 00:21:45,190
I'll tell them we don't need 
to live in hiding anymore.

294
00:21:45,610 --> 00:21:48,820
I'll tell them this is the world 
Mother Fortuna told us about!

295
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:55,390
I'll sing my dreams until my throat goes dry,

296
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:58,400
so Mother up in the skies above can hear me!

297
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:03,420
I'll tell her that I'm going to live 
happily in the world she loved!

298
00:22:06,010 --> 00:22:07,280
I see.

299
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:09,400
I understand now.

300
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:12,930
I thought I did before, 
but this exceeds my expectations.

301
00:22:13,550 --> 00:22:18,260
You are just that pushy, insolent, 
egotistical, and selfish.

302
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:20,100
The pinnacle of hypocrisy.

303
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:21,870
True. Is that bad?

304
00:22:23,170 --> 00:22:24,940
Your trial is now over.

305
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:28,250
However egotistical its ending may be,

306
00:22:28,250 --> 00:22:30,320
it has most definitely settled your past.

307
00:22:30,930 --> 00:22:34,000
Keep using your mother's sacrifice 
as an excuse for your resolve

308
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,000
to see your selfish wish 
through to the very end.

309
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:39,450
Say whatever you want.

310
00:22:39,450 --> 00:22:42,210
I'm used to your insults by now.

311
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:46,890
Two trials remain.

312
00:22:46,890 --> 00:22:50,490
I'd like to say I look forward to 
how pathetically you struggle...

313
00:22:50,490 --> 00:22:53,710
Huh? Wait, there are still more trials?

314
00:22:53,710 --> 00:22:55,720
Two more? So three in all?

315
00:22:56,210 --> 00:22:57,420
The remaining trials...

316
00:22:57,420 --> 00:22:59,790
I doubt they will pose a challenge to you.

317
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:01,700
Really?

318
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:05,100
Now that you're fighting back, 
they'll be a very poor fit.

319
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:08,140
In a sense, you've abandoned all thought.

320
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:09,610
That's super mean.

321
00:23:13,410 --> 00:23:15,370
Well, I hate you.

322
00:23:17,060 --> 00:23:20,460
But I don't hate you nearly as much.

323
00:23:42,850 --> 00:23:45,170
Thank you... so much.

324
00:23:50,910 --> 00:23:53,660
I'm sorry, Mother.

325
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:02,940
Mother...

326
00:24:04,760 --> 00:24:05,900
Mother...

327
00:24:06,590 --> 00:24:11,590
The Permafrost of Elior Forest

328
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:16,560
Sorry to push you like that,

329
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:18,880
but you told me far more than I expected.

330
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:19,810
Thanks.

331
00:24:20,320 --> 00:24:23,850
I always feared that removing 
the barrier would

332
00:24:23,850 --> 00:24:29,820
trample upon the wishes of 
Ryuzu Meyer, our progenitor.

333
00:24:29,820 --> 00:24:31,610
I get how you feel.

334
00:24:31,610 --> 00:24:35,760
But when Emilia pulls it off 
and everything works out,

335
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:39,540
we'll be able to call the 
whole world a Sanctuary.

336
00:24:40,450 --> 00:24:42,890
I leave it to you, Young Su.

337
00:24:44,850 --> 00:24:48,800
Your wish of four hundred 
years is on me now.

338
00:24:49,310 --> 00:24:51,820
Anyway, I'd like to let Shima-san rest.

339
00:24:52,260 --> 00:24:54,510
Ram, can you take care of things now?

340
00:24:54,510 --> 00:24:59,500
Oh, Old Hag Shi's hideout would be better 
than Old Hag Ryu's place for that.

341
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:00,870
I'll go with—

342
00:25:00,870 --> 00:25:02,370
Whoa, wait a second!

343
00:25:02,370 --> 00:25:04,520
You shouldn't push yourself yet, either.

344
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:07,140
We should let Ram-san and 
Ryuzu-san handle it.

345
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:07,860
Huh?

346
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:10,460
Garfiel, a boor like you 
charging at Shima-sama

347
00:25:10,460 --> 00:25:14,370
and interrupting her rest 
would defeat the purpose.

348
00:25:14,370 --> 00:25:17,500
Then I suppose I should go, too.

349
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:19,860
I would appreciate that very much.

350
00:25:19,860 --> 00:25:24,980
I would feel guilty leaving Ryuzu-sama in 
the care of two men who lack any empathy.

351
00:25:24,980 --> 00:25:26,400
That's right.

352
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:28,880
Wait, were you counting 
me as one of those m—

353
00:25:30,310 --> 00:25:34,120
I guess Ram-san must have sensed it, huh?

354
00:25:34,660 --> 00:25:37,090
Well, the fact that she overlooked...

355
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:42,070
No, the fact that she was willing to 
help us at all meant there was hope.

356
00:25:42,070 --> 00:25:44,680
Hey, don't go understanding 
each other like that!

357
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:48,850
Don't ignore me like one 
guy among ten morgrelo!

358
00:25:49,140 --> 00:25:51,450
We'd be stuck if you left,

359
00:25:51,450 --> 00:25:54,690
and since Ram is an unknown variable, 
I wanted her out of the group.

360
00:25:54,690 --> 00:25:57,210
Ram? Hang on!

361
00:25:57,210 --> 00:25:59,880
I don't understand a damn 
thing you're sayin' anymo—

362
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:03,040
We're on our way to visit Margrave Mathers.

363
00:26:03,380 --> 00:26:03,940
Huh?

364
00:26:03,940 --> 00:26:07,160
You have two arms, plus both 
of us dragging you down.

365
00:26:07,820 --> 00:26:09,680
That should be enough to get there, right?

366
00:26:10,100 --> 00:26:15,010
We need to make it back before Emilia 
comes out of there all proud.

367
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:23,340
Never did I expect you to pay 
me a visit at a time like this.

368
00:26:23,930 --> 00:26:27,060
And what brings you here?

369
00:26:27,280 --> 00:26:30,260
Look at you, greeting us in full makeup.

370
00:26:30,260 --> 00:26:32,520
It's embarrassing when you're 
that eager to see us.

371
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:36,240
Was it not you who said to me

372
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:40,820
that the next time we met, 
I should be in full makeup?

373
00:26:40,820 --> 00:26:43,570
Yeah, I guess I did say that.

374
00:26:43,570 --> 00:26:49,730
Besides, this makeup is my way of 
preparing for a battle I cannot lose.

375
00:26:49,730 --> 00:26:53,170
I see. So it's literally your war paint.

376
00:26:53,170 --> 00:26:56,840
Well, Subaru-kun? What brings you here?

377
00:26:57,140 --> 00:26:59,190
I think you know by now

378
00:26:59,190 --> 00:27:02,640
that the game board you've 
set up is falling apart.

379
00:27:03,870 --> 00:27:05,370
Yes, indeed.

380
00:27:05,730 --> 00:27:09,140
Seeing who you've brought with you 
tells me the situation has changed.

381
00:27:09,820 --> 00:27:14,620
They certainly have tamed you,
 haven't they, Garfiel?

382
00:27:14,620 --> 00:27:15,650
What?

383
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:19,650
But the one that concerns me the most is...

384
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:22,820
You mean... me?

385
00:27:23,140 --> 00:27:26,020
From the moment you entered, I wondered,

386
00:27:26,020 --> 00:27:29,500
"Just who is he, anyway?"

387
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:31,420
Damn, Otto!

388
00:27:31,420 --> 00:27:34,450
You actually got left out of the 
prophecy foretelling the future!

389
00:27:34,450 --> 00:27:36,100
That doesn't make me happy at all,

390
00:27:36,100 --> 00:27:38,800
and I can't hide my shock at how 
little sense this all makes!

391
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:43,590
And someone like this is here as a witness 
to the battle between Subaru-kun and me.

392
00:27:44,230 --> 00:27:47,310
I see. That must mean he...

393
00:27:47,650 --> 00:27:49,250
Yeah, that's right.

394
00:27:49,250 --> 00:27:51,190
The first gear's been 
thrown out of alignment.

395
00:27:51,490 --> 00:27:51,950
Huh?

396
00:27:51,950 --> 00:27:55,200
The game board you've been 
setting up so carefully

397
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:57,460
has been invaded by an unknown piece.

398
00:27:57,460 --> 00:27:59,370
That's changed the flow of things...

399
00:27:59,940 --> 00:28:04,570
thanks to my insignificant friend here,
 who isn't even in the prophecy.

400
00:28:06,340 --> 00:28:09,290
Why don't you tell me your name again?

401
00:28:14,710 --> 00:28:16,750
My name is Otto Suwen.

402
00:28:17,460 --> 00:28:21,970
I'm honored to have this 
opportunity to meet you.

403
00:28:22,470 --> 00:28:25,850
I'm only a humble merchant, but I thank you.

404
00:28:26,350 --> 00:28:28,710
I shall remember that, Otto-kun.

405
00:28:29,340 --> 00:28:33,060
The next time we meet, 
I will not overlook you.

406
00:28:33,250 --> 00:28:34,740
Good for you, Otto!

407
00:28:34,740 --> 00:28:38,320
You left a bigger impression on Roswaal 
than ever, just like you wanted!

408
00:28:38,320 --> 00:28:42,190
This wasn't how I wanted him 
to remember me, though!

409
00:28:42,830 --> 00:28:45,780
So, thanks to Otto-kun, 
you made it back on your feet

410
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:49,490
and found the backbone you 
needed for this last battle.

411
00:28:49,760 --> 00:28:51,160
That's right.

412
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:54,560
Doesn't it seem kinda weird, though?

413
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:58,020
It should be the main heroine 
that gets me back on my feet.

414
00:28:58,020 --> 00:29:00,830
Why would a male character play 
that role? How dense can you be?

415
00:29:00,830 --> 00:29:03,860
Don't look at me like it's my fault!
 I don't know, either!

416
00:29:03,860 --> 00:29:05,910
I'm just kidding, man.

417
00:29:07,190 --> 00:29:11,060
I will ask once more. 
What have you come here for?

418
00:29:17,050 --> 00:29:18,520
To advise you to surrender.

419
00:29:20,390 --> 00:29:22,650
Shima-san told me the real reason

420
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:28,290
why this Sanctuary was created.

421
00:29:28,290 --> 00:29:38,290


